    "id": "p58-q7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "Simplify the following.\n\n$$\\dfrac{\\dfrac1x+1}{\\dfrac1x-1}$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\dfrac{x+1}{1-x}$, $x\\ne0,1$.",
      "worked": "Multiply the top and bottom by $x$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\dfrac{\\dfrac1x+1}{\\dfrac1x-1}&=\\dfrac{x(\\dfrac1x+1)}{x(\\dfrac1x-1)}\\\\\\dfrac{\\dfrac1x+1}{\\dfrac1x-1}&=\\dfrac{x+1}{1-x}.\\end{align*}$$\nThe original expression requires $x\\ne0$ and $\\dfrac1x-1\\ne0$, so $x\\ne0,1$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 24
  },
